---
// A marked-off aside carrying engineer-audience material: the book's convention
// is that the main prose speaks to the primary (non-engineering) reader and the
// named-technique / industry-vocabulary detail lives in a skippable box. The
// mono "For engineers" label and thin ember-tinted rule signal "safe to skip"
// without shouting. Styling lives in PostLayout's <style> under `.post-aside`.
---
<aside class="post-aside post-aside--engineers" role="note" aria-label="For engineers">
  <p class="post-aside__label">For engineers</p>
  <div class="post-aside__body">
    <slot />
  </div>
</aside>
